## Context
Reported by the DOIfetch session (raid f9e483, 2026-10-29) through the inter-project protocol; causes as its team lead stated them, not re-verified here.
In DOIfetch no `reference-transaction` hook is installed and `core.hooksPath` is unset, so
`.git/idh/after-merge.log` never appears: nothing checks main after a merge
(`skills/merge/SKILL.md` step 9 assumes the hook starts the runner). A red main goes unseen.

## Scope
Find how a consumer project gets the hook (idh install, project setup, merge-gate enablement) and
make a gated consumer project carry it, or make `main_sweep.py --after` report the missing hook.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A gated consumer project starts the after-merge runner on a main move, or the absence is reported by lair/yawn
- [ ] Checked in DOIfetch
